# The generated verification report. A 7 MB binary of a local instance's state,
# regenerable from .verification/, and not needed to build or run ARGUS.
ARGUS-Verification-Report.pdf

# Verification evidence: screenshots and captures taken while checking a phase
# against the running stack. Kept on disk because they are what a claim of
# "verified" is backed by, and kept out of the repository because they are
# large binaries of a local instance rather than anything needed to build or
# run ARGUS.
.verification/

# Internal audit and phase records. Kept on disk because they are the working
# record of what was found, decided and deliberately left undone — and kept out
# of the repository because they are an unsparing internal assessment of this
# project, not documentation of how it works. `docs/` is the published, current
# description of the system; this directory is the notebook behind it.
docs/production-audit/
